{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tree decomposition by the minimum fill-in heuristic: repeatedly eliminate the vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose neighbors lack the fewest edges to form a clique, making them one; stop when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"remaining vertices form a clique. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"width"},{"text":" is an upper bound on the treewidth, and is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the treewidth of a chordal graph.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/treewidthminfillin()"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/treewidthMinFillIn()"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"treewidthMinFillIn","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/TreeDecomposition","text":"TreeDecomposition","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques17TreeDecompositionV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Among vertices of equal fill-in, the one of least degree, then earliest in "},{"type":"